/T (Decomposition is a fundamental skill that allows you to tackle complex tasks more efficiently. By learning to divide a large problem into smaller, more manageable parts, students develop the ability to plan, organize, and delegate tasks within group projects, while improving time management. This approach not only facilitates problem solving, but also fosters confidence, autonomy, and efficiency when facing new challenges.)
