/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (When a problem can be divided into several smaller parts, we often discover that some of these share common elements or characteristics. Even when they are not identical, they may resemble parts of other problems that we have already solved. Identifying these similarities makes it easier to understand and manage each component. Pattern recognition consists precisely of detecting these regularities and taking advantage of previous experience to address new situations more efficiently. This skill is very useful for making decisions and managing different contexts or challenges more easily.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
