/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (For example, if you have ever learned a new language, you know how important patterns are. At first, understanding and memorizing vocabulary or grammar rules can be slow and complex. However, as you progress, you begin to identify recurring patterns, such as similar sentence structures or verb conjugations. This recognition allows you to learn new vocabulary more easily and apply grammar rules more accurately in different contexts. Ultimately, the initial experience provides you with tools and patterns that, over time, increase your efficiency and your ability to solve problems.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
